[N 40-40 Level 40: Ironforge]
[D Forever Shaman 30-60 (Braedyn)\\Level 40 in Ironforge: Bring the Light to Benedictus by tram, Eldrun's ranks with Windfury Weapon 2, Mail, Artisan Skinning, the Uldaman pickups at Stormpike and Krom, then riding and a ram at Amberstill Ranch on the road to Thelsamar.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel check|r  -  this chapter wants level 40: Windfury Weapon rank 2 and the other level-40 ranks, Mail (client SkillRaceClassInfo row 145: MinLevel 40), Apprentice Riding and the ram all need it. Still 39? Train the 38 ranks you lack, take the two Uldaman quests and go on to Uldaman (chapter 39e): its mobs ding you there. The Platinum Discs (2278) need level 40 when you speak to the Discs behind Archaedas - if you are still 39 at that point, skip them (2278, 2279 and 2439 go). Back in Ironforge at the end of 39e, come back to Eldrun for the level-40 row and Mail, and walk out to Amberstill Ranch for riding before you hearth
[OC]|cffffffffIronforge|r  -  you start in the Hall of Explorers where chapter 39c left you (554 handed in at Prospector Stormpike), hearth = Farholde Keep and it stays there. One hand-in at most (4,300 XP), then training, the Uldaman pickups and the ride out to Thelsamar
[OC]|cffffcc00Carried in:|r Bring the Light (3636, complete) only if you took it at level 39 in chapter 39 and killed Amnennar in 39b. Still carried: The Riverglades Report (95315, chapter 40) and, if the Field Marshal's Log dropped, 94887 (chapter 40)
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Training:|r no stop since chapter 37, so the level 38 row is usually still open; chapter 35 bought it only if you were 38 there

[OC]|cffffffffStormwind by tram|r  -  only with Bring the Light in your log; without it there is no Stormwind trip
[O] Take the Deeprun Tram at the far east end of Tinker Town to Stormwind (only if you took Bring the Light in chapter 39) [G76,51 Ironforge]
[O] In the Cathedral of Light at [TAR1284 Archbishop Benedictus], [QT3636] (4,300 XP, no money) [G50.3,45.5 Stormwind City]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear (3636):|r |cff66ff66Amberglow Talisman|r (neck +1 Agi +7 Sta +10 Spi, 26.1 on the weights) or the Purified Ring (+12 Int, +5 spell damage; 24.3). The ring would replace the Tiger Band (22.5) beside the Coldwater Ring (26.1, chapter 39c), a gain of 1.8. Take the Amberglow if your neck scores under 24.3, otherwise the Purified Ring in place of the Tiger Band. Vanquisher's Sword (fixed reward) is a one-hand sword you cannot use: vendor it (1g 80s 3c)
[O] Take the Deeprun Tram back to Ironforge (the big building at the back of the Dwarven District) [G73.1,49.2 Stormwind City]

[OC]|cffffffffIronforge|r  -  Eldrun in the Forlorn Cavern, Balthus in the Great Forge, then the Hall of Explorers
[A Shaman] In the Forlorn Cavern at [TAR258098 Eldrun Stormbreaker], [T] train every rank your level allows that the sheet marks must or buy (level 38 row if not bought yet: buys Strength of Earth Totem 3, Flametongue Totem 2 - 1g 10s each; when gold is easy: Lightning Bolt 7 - 1g 10s; level 40 row, only at 40: must Windfury Weapon 2, buys Healing Wave 7, Searing Totem 4 - 1g 20s each, Call of the Spirits - 1g 26s 31c; when gold is easy: Lightning Shield 5, Flame Shock 4 - 1g 20s each; both rows 7g 6s 31c in all). Still 39: the 40 row waits for the end of chapter 39e [G47.1,13.8 Ironforge]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Imbue:|r Windfury Weapon on the two-hander from now on (the weights doc rates Rockbiter and Windfury within 2% at 40; Windfury is the pick)
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Mail:|r the client lets shamans learn Mail at 40 (SkillRaceClassInfo row 145, MinLevel 40), but Eldrun's Wowhead list has no Mail entry. Ask Eldrun for Mail; if he does not list it, open your skills - it may come by itself at 40 (|cffffcc00unverified|r). Mail you carried from earlier chapters goes on now: the Excavator Gauntlets (36.0, chapter 35) beat the Prospector Gloves (27.5) but not the Traveled Gloves (40.0)
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Talents 38-40:|r the sheet says Mindfulness 3/3; the weights doc says put one point in at 38 and test whether it stacks with Improved Stormstrike (|cffffcc00unverified|r)
[O]At [TAR6291 Balthus Stoneflayer] in the Great Forge, [T] learn Artisan Skinning (5g) once Skinning is 200 [G39.9,32.5 Ironforge]
[OC]|cffffcc00Mageweave:|r count your Mageweave Cloth before you leave Ironforge. Brother Lowley's Wound Dressings at the start of chapter 40 takes 20 and opens his and Sister Rowland's chain (10,865 XP): if you hold fewer, buy the rest at the Ironforge Auction House now (its position is not in the data, unverified)
In the Hall of Explorers at [TAR1356 Prospector Stormpike], [QA2398 The Lost Dwarves] (315 XP, requires level 35: find Baelog inside Uldaman - carried to chapter 39e) [G74.6,11.7 Ironforge]
At [TAR6294 Krom Stoutarm] beside him, [QA1360 Reclaimed Treasures] (3,600 XP, requires level 33: Krom Stoutarm's Treasure from his chest in Uldaman's North Common Hall, back to him here - carried to chapter 39e) [G74.2,9.4 Ironforge]

[OC]|cffffcc00Gold check:|r the mount is Apprentice Riding at Ultham Ironhorn, 100g at Friendly (Wowhead raw 1,052,631 c, x0.95) or 94g 74s at Honored. The ram itself is the reward of Your First Riding Ram at Veron Amberstill (in the quest data since 12 Nov, |cffffcc00unverified|r in game); the rams he sells are listed at 20g and at 40g on Wowhead. Train when you have the gold and are 40; the route works on foot to 43
[OC]|cffffffffAmberstill Ranch|r  -  no mount money, or still 39: take the flight line below and skip the ranch steps
[O]At [TAR1573 Gryth Thurden], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Thelsamar]|r - only if you are not buying riding now [G55.5,47.7 Ironforge]
[O] Walk out of Ironforge and east down the Dun Morogh road to Amberstill Ranch [G63.5,50.6 Dun Morogh]
[O]At [TAR4772 Ultham Ironhorn], [QA97018 Learning to Ride] and [T] train Apprentice Riding at Friendly or better (price in the gold check above; the ram tooltip says "Requires Ram Riding" and his Wowhead list "Apprentice Riding", |cffffcc00unverified|r) [G63.8,50.1 Dun Morogh]
[O]At [TAR1261 Veron Amberstill], [QT97018] [QA97017 Your First Riding Ram] (inspect his three rams, then choose one as the reward; whether he offers it before Learning to Ride is handed in is |cffffcc00unverified|r) [G63.5,50.6 Dun Morogh]
[O]Inspect the [TAR267474 White Ram], the [TAR267473 Brown Ram] and the [TAR267475 Gray Ram] in the pen beside him [QC97017] [G64.0,50.4 Dun Morogh]
[O]At [TAR1261 Veron Amberstill], [QT97017] (1,550 XP) and choose your Brown, Gray or White Ram (requires level 40) [G63.5,50.6 Dun Morogh]
Ride (or walk) east through the South Gate into Loch Modan and on to Thelsamar (the road from the ranch is |cffffcc00unverified|r) [G33.9,51.0 Loch Modan]
